  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Which of the following numbers are surds?\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{144},\\,\\sqrt{25},\\,\\sqrt{74}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "A surd is a number containing a radical symbol $\\sqrt{}$ that cannot be written as a positive or negative whole number or fraction.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each number in turn.\n\n- $\\sqrt{144}$ is **NOT** a surd. Since  $144$ is a perfect square, we can get rid of the square root symbol $(\\sqrt{})$ and obtain a whole number: \n\n$$\n\\sqrt{144}=\\sqrt{{12}^{2}}=12\n$$\n\n- $\\sqrt{25}$ is **NOT** a surd. Since $25$  is a perfect square, we can get rid of the square root symbol $(\\sqrt{})$ and obtain a whole number: \n\n$$\n\\sqrt{25}=\\sqrt{{5}^{2}}=5\n$$\n\n- $\\sqrt{74}$ is a surd because $74$ is not a perfect square. In fact $\\sqrt{74}=8.602\\text{ }325\\,...$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is: $\\sqrt{74}$ only.",
